### 5.5.4 HISTORICAL FORM-SPECIFIC RULES (NON-AUTHORITATIVE)

**HISTORICAL ONLY:** The forms below are retained as provenance and must not be
used for current dose arithmetic. Obtain the current form, carrier, fraction,
and concentration basis from the pinned inventory runtime first.

| Material | Your Form | Effective Dilution | Rule |
|----------|-----------|-------------------|------|
| Ambroxan/Ambrox Super | 10% in DPG | 10× | When formula says "5% ambroxan" → use **50%** of your solution |
| Beta Damascone | 10% in DPG | 10× | Formula 0.5% → Use 5% of your solution |
| Ionone Beta | 10% in DPG | 10× | Formula 0.3% → Use 3% of your solution |
| Coumarin | 10% in DPG | 10× | Formula 2% → Use 20% of your solution (IFRA limit accounts for dilution!) |
| Skatole | 1% in DPG | 100× | Formula 0.005% → Use 0.5% of your solution |
| Indole | 10% in DPG | 10× | Formula 0.05% → Use 0.5% of your solution |
| E2MB | 1:1000 | 1000× | Trace use only; 0.01% of this = 0.00001% actual |
| Galaxolide | 80% in DPG | 1.25× | Near-neat; account for 80% actual |
| Ethyl Maltol | 5%/1% in ethanol | 20×/100× | Powerful; 1% solution is easier to dose |
| Saffron FTEC | 10% in DPG | 10× | Formula 0.5% → Use 5% of your solution |
| Benzoin Siam | 50% in DPG | 2× | Formula 2% → Use 4% of your solution |
| Alpha-Irone | 3% in DEP/IPM | 33× | Formula 1% → Use 33% of your solution |

**DILUTION CALCULATION:**
```
Actual % in formula = (% of diluted solution used) × (concentration)
Example: 5% of 10% Ambroxan → 5% × 0.10 = 0.5% actual ambroxan
```

